Z||000000||The Fieromaster||07-06-2001||11:11 AM||||Having a glowing manifold problem on the firewall side of my 2.8L... Wondering what is causing this... Why is it only on the firewall side??<P>Help is greatly appreciated...<P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That Wrecked Better"<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">    <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||5
Z||000001||Formula88||07-06-2001||11:15 AM||||Glowing manifold?  Down on power?  Could be a clogged cat.  Lean mixture.  EGR?  My vote would be check the cat first.||||reg||4
Z||000002||88CoupeV6||07-06-2001||11:18 AM||||or a leak in the manifold.<P>------------------<BR>Josh <B>(known by TheFiero64 for first 1239 posts)</B><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">    <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||4
Z||000003||DRH||07-06-2001||11:25 AM||||Check the EGR tube that runs from under the EGR to the intake manifold. These are notorious for deteriorating and developing serious vacuum leaks. Since it feeds into the the firewall side of the intake, those cylinders run much leaner and cause just that side to glow.||||reg||1
Z||000004||86SE||07-06-2001||01:28 PM||||Mine used to glow.  So I put on a new EGR valve and it solved that problem.  But both of my manifolds were glowing.....<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://fierodude.hypermart.net/mysig.jpg"> <BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero -- 3.4L Conversion *SUSPENDED* --<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fiero_24||07-06-2001||02:25 PM||||Check this first.  I have had this problem with the ECM on my current Fiero, but the evaporative fuel canister went out on my 86 Coupe and caused the manifold to glow.  At night take off the hose from the top valve from the evaporative fuel canister and plug it with something (I used a Spark plug), and see if the glowing goes away.  If not, then put the tibe back on and change the EGR.  The reason the canister does this same problem is because the purge vaulve goes out and starts sucking fuel out of the tank instead of the fuel vapors.  By taking the tube off you keep it from suckng extra fuel, you prevent it from dumping too much fuel in the cylinders.  DO NOT DRIVE WITH THE HOSE OFF OF THE CANISTER!  If the canister is bad and sucking fuel you will create a fire hazard.  In my opinion it is ok to do it at idle in your driveway.  If anyone else has any opinions on this please let me know, or correct me if I am wrong.  I have had to replace the canister in 2 different cars 4cyl and V6 (autozone special order $34), and I never had the glowing manifold problem after that.<P>Craig<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT<p>[This message has been edited by Fiero_24 (edited 07-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||My7Fieros||07-06-2001||07:51 PM||||All I can say is good luck...Ive got an 87 GT w/ the same prob and Ive done absolutly EVERYTHING and they still glow....who knows. M7F||||reg||1
Z||000007||Wrench||07-06-2001||11:12 PM||||Check your fuel pump pressure. My 86 GT had the same problem and I found the pump was shot. Hope this helps||||reg||1
Z||000008||The Fieromaster||07-06-2001||11:30 PM||||Well....the cat is clogged....but it is in the dumpster <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> and the manafolds are glowing.  The fuel pump is new.  The EGR Tube is good, well, MINT, so I am sure that is not the problem.  Could it be a vacuume leak somewere else?  How about the EGR being shot itself?  <P>I was also wondering if timing has something to do with it?  Just a thought.<P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That Wrecked Better"<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">    <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||1
Z||000009||FieroJoe||07-07-2001||12:39 AM||||To check and see if your EGR works, put your fingers under the valve until you can feel the diaphragmn.  Rev the engine and feel if the valve moves.  It should move up as more vacuum is applied to it (more revs more vac).  If it doesnt, it's probably shot.  Also, check the EGR vac line itself to make sure that the valve is getting the correct vacuum applied to it.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
